allmatrix}A&*\\\\0&0\\end{smallmatrix}\\right]$ with $A\\in V$. We prove the wildness of the problem of classifying Lie algebras $\\widetilde V$ with the bracket operation","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Tetiana Klymchuk","Anatolii P. Petravchuk"],"year":"2017"},"arXiv:1701.08826":{"abstract":"W.Specht (1940) proved that two $n\\times n$ complex matrices $A$ and $B$ are unitarily similar if and only if $\\operatorname{trace} w(A,A^{\\ast}) = \\operatorname{trace} w(B,B^{\\ast})$ for every word $w(x,y)$ in two noncommuting variables. We extend his criterion and its generalizations by N.A.Wiegmann (1961) and N.Jing (2015) to an arbitrary system $\\mathcal A$ consisting of complex or real inner ","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Roger A. Horn","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2017"},"arXiv:1403.2645":{"abstract":"We give a method for constructing a regularizing decomposition of a matrix pencil, which is formulated in terms of the linear mappings. We prove that two pencils are topologically equivalent if and only if their regularizing decompositions coincide up to permutation of summands and their regular parts coincide up to homeomorphisms of their spaces.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Tetiana Rybalkina","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2014"},"arXiv:1004.3590":{"abstract":"We construct the Hasse diagrams $G_2$ and $G_3$ for the closure ordering on the sets of congruence classes of $2\\times 2$ and $3\\times 3$ complex matrices. In other words, we construct two directed graphs whose vertices are $2\\times 2$ or, respectively, $3\\times 3$ canonical matrices under congruence and there is a directed path from $A$ to $B$ if and only if $A$ can be transformed by an arbitrari","authors":["Andrii Dmytryshyn","Vyacheslav Futorny","Bo Kågström"],"year":"2010"},"arXiv:0710.0810":{"abstract":"Tridiagonal canonical forms of square matrices under congruence or *congruence, pairs of symmetric or skew-symmetric matrices under congruence, and pairs of Hermitian matrices under *congruence are given over an algebraically closed field of characteristic different from 2.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Roger A. Horn","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:0710.0928":{"abstract":"We give canonical matrices of bilinear or sesquilinear forms UxV-->C, (V/U)xV-->C, in which V is a vector space over the field C of complex numbers and U is its subspace.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:0710.0954":{"abstract":"We give a canonical form for a complex matrix, whose square is normal, under transformations of unitary similarity as well as a canonical form for a real matrix, whose square is normal, under transformations of orthogonal similarity.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Roger A. Horn","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:1304.5762":{"abstract":"We study how small perturbations of a 2-by-2 complex matrix can change its canonical form for *congruence. We construct the Hasse diagram for the closure ordering on the set of *congruence classes of 2-by-2 matrices.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Lena Klimenko","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2013"},"arXiv:2406.05492":{"abstract":"In this paper we introduce the shifted twisted Yangian of type {\\sf AI}, following the work of Lu--Wang--Zhang, and we study their semiclassical limits, a class of Poisson algebras. We demonstrate that they coincide with the Dirac reductions of the semiclassical shifted Yangian for $\\mathfrak{gl}_n$. We deduce that these shifted twisted Yangians admit truncations which are isomorphic to Slodowy sl","authors":["Lukas Tappeiner","Lewis Topley"],"year":"2024"},"arXiv:1112.3682":{"abstract":"A square matrix is nonderogatory if its Jordan blocks have distinct eigenvalues. We give canonical forms (i) for nonderogatory complex matrices up to unitary similarity and (ii) for pairs of complex matrices up to similarity, in which one matrix has distinct eigenvalues. The types of these canonical forms are given by undirected and, respectively, directed graphs with no undirected cycles.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Roger A. Horn","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2011"},"arXiv:1907.03213":{"abstract":"Our purpose is to give new proofs of several known results about perturbations of matrix pencils. Andrzej Pokrzywa (1986) described the closure of orbit of a Kronecker canonical pencil $A-λB$ in terms of inequalities with pencil invariants. In more detail, Pokrzywa described all Kronecker canonical pencils $K-λL$ such that each neighborhood of $A-λB$ contains a pencil whose Kronecker canonical for","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Tetiana Klymchuk","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2019"}}}